WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:03.320
What real criminal case inspired the character
of Eddie Munson?

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.359
And what does Eleven have in common with Luke
Skywalker?

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.420
Keep watching for Easter eggs you might have
missed in Season 4, Volume 2 of Stranger Things.

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:11.420
But beware!

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:12.519
There are spoilers ahead.

00:00:13.679 --> 00:00:17.370
When speaking with Netflix's Tudum, the Duffer
brothers hinted at the fact that Eddie Munson

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:21.720
is inspired by a specific person who was a
Dungeons &amp; Dragons fanatic and metalhead just

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:22.770
like Eddie.

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:26.820
A tweet from Netflix Geeked confirmed that
Eddie Munson is loosely based on West Memphis

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.420
Three member Damien Echols.

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:32.839
A writer and artist these days, Echols was
one of three teenagers convicted under highly

00:00:32.839 --> 00:00:37.340
dubious circumstances of the 1993 murders
of Steve Branch, Michael Moore, and Christopher

00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:41.730
Byers, in what the media considered at the
time to be satanic rituals.

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:45.239
Echols had a tendency for dressing in black
and listening to heavy metal, which led the

00:00:45.239 --> 00:00:49.350
community to ostracize him and believe he
conducted spiritual practices with ties to

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:51.289
witchcraft and satanism.

00:00:51.289 --> 00:00:53.909
In an interview about Season 4, Ross Duffer
said,

00:00:53.909 --> 00:00:57.579
"Something we really wanted to get into this
year was the Satanic Panic."

00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:01.930
The term "Satanic Panic" refers to a period
in the '80s and '90s when society began blaming

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:06.320
its various ills on the influence of heavy
metal music and fantastical imagery from escapist

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.049
entertainment like Dungeons &amp; Dragons.

00:01:09.049 --> 00:01:13.350
Advocates of the Satanic Panic were specifically
concerned about supposed satanists harming

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:14.719
or sacrificing small children.

00:01:14.719 --> 00:01:20.180
"There's a widely held opinion that what happened
at the daycare was the devil's handiwork."

00:01:20.180 --> 00:01:23.530
The West Memphis Three were released from
prison in 2011.

00:01:23.530 --> 00:01:27.079
Echols went on to become a New York Times
bestselling author and produced a documentary

00:01:27.079 --> 00:01:28.250
about his experience.

00:01:28.250 --> 00:01:31.140
When describing the character of Eddie, Matt
Duffer said,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:34.571
"What's sad about his narrative is that the
people who get to know him love him, and the

00:01:34.571 --> 00:01:36.310
people who don't have judged him horribly."

00:01:37.750 --> 00:01:41.520
It's no secret that the creators of Stranger
Things love to pay respect to horror classics

00:01:41.520 --> 00:01:45.240
with the numerous references they sprinkle
throughout the series, and Season 4 is no

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.240
different.

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.010
At one point, Joyce and Hopper come across
a Russian lab of tanks filled with Demogorgons

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:54.719
for experimentation, and the scene is almost
identical to one in Alien: Resurrection — a

00:01:54.719 --> 00:01:58.520
1997 movie that, just like Stranger Things,
co-stars Winona Ryder.

00:01:58.520 --> 00:02:00.999
However, the Duffer brothers didn't stop there.

00:02:00.999 --> 00:02:04.749
There are several other nods to the Alien
film franchise throughout the season, such

00:02:04.749 --> 00:02:06.880
as Paul Reiser's use of the word "kiddo."

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:11.580
Burke, Reiser's character in Aliens, also
makes frequent use of the patronizing nickname.

00:02:11.580 --> 00:02:15.230
References to the Stephen King horror classic,
Carrie appear throughout the season as well,

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:18.600
like when El gets bullied in front of her
whole school and when Max's happy memory of

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.510
the Winter Ball is ruined by blood-filled
balloons.

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:24.720
The Duffer brothers have confirmed that when
planning this season, they focused a lot on

00:02:24.720 --> 00:02:28.129
A Nightmare on Elm Street, Hellraiser and
the It miniseries.

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:31.660
They also said they modeled Vecna after Pinhead
from Hellraiser.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:34.049
"It's time."

00:02:34.049 --> 00:02:42.010
And, of course, Robert Englund plays Henry's
father, Victor Creel, which means Vecna's

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:43.720
dad is pretty much Freddy Krueger.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.459
Those final two episodes of Vol. 2 are extremely
action packed, but did you notice a familiar

00:02:49.459 --> 00:02:51.500
weapon amid all of the chaos?

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.490
As revealed by David Harbour on his personal
Instagram page, the sword used by Hopper to

00:02:55.490 --> 00:02:59.250
slay the Demogorgon in the final episode is
actually the same Atlantean sword famously

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:02.700
used by Arnold Schwarzenegger in the Conan
the Barbarian films.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:06.510
Harbour describes the prop as both, quote,
"heavy as hell" and, "a tremendous honor to

00:03:06.510 --> 00:03:07.510
wield."

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:10.790
Fans also pointed out some foreshadowing to
this epic sword battle that came in the first

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:12.310
episode of Season 4.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:15.769
When we get a glimpse of Mike's bedroom, a
poster for Conan the Barbarian can be seen

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:17.310
hanging on his wall.

00:03:17.310 --> 00:03:20.690
This tiny Easter egg probably wouldn't have
meant anything to you prior to the finale

00:03:20.690 --> 00:03:21.900
episode with Hopper.

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:25.610
Schwarzenegger himself actually admitted to
still owning the legendary sword and keeping

00:03:25.610 --> 00:03:27.090
it in his office.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:30.909
When asked if he still had the sword back
in 2010, the actor and onetime Governor of

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:33.210
California confirmed that he, in fact, did.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:38.110
Eddie plays a vital role in the final moments
of the fight with Vecna by sacrificing himself

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:39.409
for the greater good.

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:43.280
In what is definitely the most metal concert
in the history of the Upside Down, Eddie shreds

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:46.030
to Metallica in order to distract the Demobats.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:49.780
The song Eddie performs, "Master of Puppets,"
is of clear significance.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:53.760
Given the way Vecna tends to toy with his
victims by forcing them to relive their worst

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:57.909
fears and traumas, Vecna is basically a metaphorical
master of puppets.

00:03:57.909 --> 00:04:01.780
Metallica actually reposted the clip on their
Instagram page, praising the show for how

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.390
well they incorporated the song.

00:04:03.390 --> 00:04:06.489
They admit to being blown away by the final
product, writing,

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:10.000
"Some folks were able to guess the song just
by seeing a few seconds of Joseph Quinn's

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:11.310
hands in the trailer."

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:14.440
Eddie's fate sadly seemed to be written in
stone from his first appearance.

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:18.930
If you look closely at Eddie's arms, you'll
see a tattoo of bats as well as another tattoo

00:04:18.930 --> 00:04:23.330
of a hand controlling a puppet on strings
— direct connections to the circumstances

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:24.710
of his inevitable death.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:27.792
"I didn't run away this time, right?"

00:04:28.389 --> 00:04:31.639
The Duffer brothers sat down with Collider
and revealed that they have taken a lot of

00:04:31.639 --> 00:04:33.979
inspiration from the Star Wars franchise.

00:04:33.979 --> 00:04:34.979
Matt Duffer said,

00:04:34.979 --> 00:04:37.639
"We always have wanted to do an 'Empire Strikes
Back' ending.

00:04:37.639 --> 00:04:39.400
We tried to do [that] with [Season 4].

00:04:39.400 --> 00:04:41.139
Where it's the sense of loss."

00:04:41.139 --> 00:04:44.930
Star Wars: Episode V – The Empire Strikes
Back is known for its shocking ending where

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.040
the bad guys more-or-less prevail.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:51.070
Sadly, Vecna likewise kind of prevails when
the Upside Down leaks into the real world

00:04:51.070 --> 00:04:52.350
of Hawkins, Indiana.

00:04:52.350 --> 00:04:56.389
There's also a similarity between Eleven and
Luke Skywalker — both characters abandon

00:04:56.389 --> 00:05:00.780
extensive training sessions against their
mentors' wishes in order to help their friends.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:04.590
In Luke's case, his decision leads to the
loss of his hand and Han Solo being taken

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:09.610
prisoner; in Eleven's, her attempt to intervene
in Vecna's plan leads to Max's coma, blinding,

00:05:09.610 --> 00:05:11.120
and possible paralysis.

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:15.050
But one must not overlook the moment when
Murray utters one of the most famous lines

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:16.750
from the entire Star Wars franchise:

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.039
"I've got a bad feeling about this."

00:05:20.190 --> 00:05:23.819
There's no denying that Tom Cruise was an
'80s heartthrob following his roles in Risky

00:05:23.819 --> 00:05:25.319
Business and Top Gun.

00:05:25.319 --> 00:05:28.990
It's safe to say that Cruise had a dedicated
fan base back in the day, and Nancy Wheeler

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:30.830
was most definitely a member.

00:05:30.830 --> 00:05:34.840
Not only does Nancy have a Tom Cruise poster
stuck on her wall as of the very first season

00:05:34.840 --> 00:05:38.759
and mentions him on several occasions — she
and Steve actually dress up as Risky Business

00:05:38.759 --> 00:05:41.340
characters for Halloween back in Season 2.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:45.310
Robin briefly teases Nancy about her poster,
which still hangs on her wall, in Season 4.

00:05:45.310 --> 00:05:48.050
"You have a Tom Cruise poster."

00:05:48.050 --> 00:05:49.050
"That's.

00:05:49.050 --> 00:05:50.050
Old."

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.710
A Reddit user also pointed out the visual
similarities between Steve from Stranger Things

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:56.520
and Steve from The Outsiders, played by Cruise.

00:05:56.520 --> 00:05:59.289
Clearly Nancy has a type, and we can't blame
her.

00:05:59.289 --> 00:06:02.840
When the gang gets together to plan their
attack on Vecna, they decide to stock up on

00:06:02.840 --> 00:06:05.099
weapons at a store called The War Zone.

00:06:05.099 --> 00:06:08.599
When Eddie points out an advertisement for
the place, we see the company's logo takes

00:06:08.599 --> 00:06:10.800
clear inspiration from the Top Gun logo.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:14.930
Mason Dye, who portrays the unhinged jock
Jason, did an interview with the Steve Varley

00:06:14.930 --> 00:06:18.449
Show and explained that Tom Cruise was the
main inspiration behind his character.

00:06:18.449 --> 00:06:19.449
He said,

00:06:19.449 --> 00:06:23.139
"I sat down with the Duffer brothers and [producer]
Shawn Levy and they were like, 'Okay, Jason

00:06:23.139 --> 00:06:25.430
is just Tom Cruise from his '80s movies.'

00:06:25.430 --> 00:06:29.390
So I just went back and watched 'Risky Business,'
'Top Gun,' like all his '80s movies a week

00:06:29.390 --> 00:06:30.390
prior to filming."

00:06:31.390 --> 00:06:35.210
In the final episodes of the season, viewers
learn that there is a large significance surrounding

00:06:35.210 --> 00:06:36.490
the number four.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:40.330
Not only does a clock chime four times whenever
Vecna is about to claim another victim, but

00:06:40.330 --> 00:06:43.849
he also requires exactly four victims to enact
his plan.

00:06:43.849 --> 00:06:48.270
In order for the Upside Down to break through
to the regular dimension, Vecna needs to create

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:51.879
four portals, which ultimately results in
the four cracks seen in the final scenes of

00:06:51.879 --> 00:06:52.879
the season.

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:56.090
While all of this is explicitly explained
throughout the series, there are some additional

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:58.270
references that aren't as noticeable.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:02.840
The main characters are all split into four
distinct groups — the Hellfire gang in Hawkins,

00:07:02.840 --> 00:07:08.160
El and Papa in the training facility, Hopper
and Joyce in Russia, and Will and co. in California.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.070
It makes this the first season where characters
fight the main antagonist simultaneously from

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:15.520
different locations across the globe and other
sides of the dimensional barrier.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:19.550
If you were so inclined, you could theorize
that the importance of the number four could

00:07:19.550 --> 00:07:24.000
relate to the four horsemen of the apocalypse,
but we can only hope more explanations unfold

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:24.774
next season.

00:07:25.323 --> 00:07:28.880
One of the best parts about Stranger Things
is dissecting the countless Easter eggs and

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:31.040
background details scattered throughout.

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:34.970
For example, while the Hawkins group scrambles
to find music to bring Nancy back from Vecna's

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:37.259
mindscape, we catch a glimpse of Eddie's bedroom.

00:07:37.259 --> 00:07:41.160
If you look closely, his walls are packed
with posters from various heavy metal bands

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:46.181
ranging from Iron Maiden, Anthrax, Judas Priest,
Slayer, and Kreator; proving he is a true

00:07:46.181 --> 00:07:47.181
metalhead.

00:07:47.181 --> 00:07:48.181
"Music!

00:07:48.181 --> 00:07:49.181
We need music!"

00:07:49.181 --> 00:07:50.740
"This is music!"

00:07:50.740 --> 00:07:54.889
An example of subtle symbolism occurs during
the moments of Brenner's death in the desert.

00:07:54.889 --> 00:07:59.050
As the camera pans over him, he can be seen
in a crucifix pose, most likely mirroring

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:01.170
the Christ-like way in which he viewed himself.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:05.289
However, the camera then flips the image upside
down in order to evoke the evil that Brenner

00:08:05.289 --> 00:08:08.340
truly created by bringing Vecna into this
world.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.680
When the Hawkins kids go to The War Zone to
stock up on weapons, they quickly pass by

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:15.470
a bulletin board covered with Wanted posters
for all the members of the Hellfire Club,

00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:19.639
showing that most of the town has succumbed
to satanic panic by this point.

00:08:19.639 --> 00:08:23.440
During this same visit, Robin catches a glimpse
of her school crush Vickie, who is sadly getting

00:08:23.440 --> 00:08:24.840
cozy with some guy.

00:08:24.840 --> 00:08:28.479
Meanwhile, there are uncanny similarities
between Vickie's wardrobe and the look of

00:08:28.479 --> 00:08:32.420
Molly Ringwald's character in Sixteen Candles,
which would have been released about three

00:08:32.420 --> 00:08:36.320
years earlier, which could imply that Vickie
is a John Hughes fan.

